{"__type":"$$EventMessageAiNode","id":"fa9505cb-9e33-473e-b81f-f5ad3e441478","ts":"2026-07-18T13:10:37.708-04:00","eventName":"n8n.ai.llm.generated","message":"n8n.ai.llm.generated","payload":{"executionId":"109","nodeName":"OpenRouter Chat Model","workflowName":"ForgeAI - Software Architect Agent","nodeType":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenRouter","workflowId":"GtMVKU0V13n1DZOO","msg":"{\"messages\":[\"System: You are ForgeAI Software Architect.\\n\\nDesign the complete software architecture.\\n\\nReturn ONLY JSON.\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"architecture\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"frontend\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"backend\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"database\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"apis\\\":[],\\n  \\\"folder_structure\\\":[],\\n  \\\"deployment\\\":\\\"\\\"\\n}\\nHuman: AI powered travel planner\"],\"options\":{\"openai_api_key\":{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"secret\",\"id\":[\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"]},\"model\":\"openai/gpt-oss-20b:free\",\"max_retries\":2,\"configuration\":{\"baseURL\":\"https://openrouter.ai/api/v1\",\"fetchOptions\":{\"dispatcher\":{\"_events\":{},\"_eventsCount\":0}}},\"model_kwargs\":{}},\"response\":{\"response\":{\"generations\":[[{\"text\":\"{\\\"architecture\\\":\\\"A modular, micro‑service based architecture with a clear separation of concerns. The system consists of a front‑end layer (React/Next.js), an API Gateway, several domain‑specific services (User, Auth, Recommendation, Planner, Booking, Payment, Analytics), a shared model inference service, a messaging layer (Kafka) for event driven flows, and persistent storage (PostgreSQL, Elasticsearch, Redis, S3). All services genocide & secure via mutual TLS. The design follows a domain‑driven design (DDD) and adheres to the 12‑factor application principles.\\\",\\\"frontend\\\":\\\"React 18 with Next.js for SSR, Tailwind CSS for styling, TypeScript for safety, React‑Query for data fetching, Redux Toolkit for global state, Mapbox GL JS for interactive maps, Stripe.js for payments. The UI consumes the API Gateway endpoints over HTTPS and supports offline caching via Service Workers. Mobile‑first responsive design and accessibility compliance.\\\",\\\"backend\\\":\\\"Node.js 20 (TypeScript) for most services using NestJS (for classic micro‑service boilerplate) and Python (FastAPI) for the ML inference service. Each service runs in an isolated Docker container, exposing gRPC endpoints for internal communication and HTTP/REST for external interactions. All services use structured logging (Pino) and have health‑check endpoints for orchestration platforms. Shared modules provide common DTOs, validation schemas, and OpenAPI spec generation.\\\",\\\"database\\\":\\\"PostgreSQL (Amazon Aurora Serverless) for relational data (users, trips, bookings). Elasticsearch for geospatial search and faceted filtering of destinations. Redis (Amazon ElastiCache) for session storage, rate‑limiting, and caching of recommendation results. AWS S3 (or MinIO) for storing media assets (photos, itineraries). A Kafka cluster for event streaming (user activity, booking updates).\\\",\\\"apis\\\":[{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Auth API\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"JWT based authentication, refresh tokens, OAuth2 with Google/Facebook.\\\",\\\"endpoints\\\":[\\\"POST /api/auth/login\\\",\\\"POST /api/auth/signup\\\",\\\"POST /api/auth/refresh\\\",\\\"POST /api/auth/logout\\\"]},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"User API\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"CRUD for user profiles and preferences.\\\",\\\"endpoints\\\":[\\\"GET /api/user/me\\\",\\\"GET /api/user/{id}\\\",\\\"PATCH /api/user/{id}\\\",\\\"DELETE /api/user/{id}\\\"]},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Destination API\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Search and filter destinations, geospatial queries.\\\",\\\"endpoints\\\":[\\\"GET /api/destinations\\\",\\\"GET /api/destinations/{id}\\\",\\\"POST /api/destinations/search\\\"]},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Recommendation API\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Return personalized destination and itinerary suggestions using the ML service.\\\",\\\"endpoints\\\":[\\\"POST /api/recommendations\\\",\\\"GET /api/recommendations/history\\\"]},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Planner API\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Create, modify, and finalize travel itineraries.\\\",\\\"endpoints\\\":[\\\"POST /api/plans\\\",\\\"GET /api/plans/{id}\\\",\\\"PATCH /api/plans/{id}\\\",\\\"DELETE /api/plans/{id}\\\"]},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Booking API\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Book hotels, flights, tours by communicating with third‑party partners via SOAP/REST.\\\" ,\\\"endpoints\\\":[\\\"POST /api/booking\\\",\\\"GET /api/booking/{id}\\\",\\\"PUT /api/booking/{id}/cancel\\\"]},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Payment API\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Process payments with Stripe and manage payment records.\\\",\\\"endpoints\\\":[\\\"POST /api/payments\\\",\\\"GET /api/payments/{id}\\\"]},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Analytics API\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Kod data for user engagementรัก.\\\",\\\"endpoints\\\":[\\\"GET /api/analytics/user-stats\\\",\\\"GET /api/analytics/trip-stats\\\"]}],\\\"folder_structure\\\":[\\\"frontend/\\\",\\\"frontend/pages/\\\",\\\"frontend/components/\\\",\\\"frontend/hooks/\\\",\\\"frontend/api/\\\",\\\"frontend/services/\\\",\\\"backend/\\\",\\\"backend/api-gateway/\\\",\\\"backend/services/auth/\\\",\\\"backend/services/user/\\\",\\\"backend/services/destination/\\\",\\\"backend/services/recommendation/\\\",\\\"backend/services/planner/\\\",\\\"backend/services/booking/\\\",\\\"backend/services/payment/\\\",\\\"backend/services/analytics/\\\",\\\"backend/shared/\\\",\\\"backend/common/\\\",\\\"backend/config/\\\",\\\"backend/models/\\\",\\\"backend/routes/\\\",\\\"backend/app.ts\\\",\\\"docker/\\\",\\\"docker-compose.yml\\\",\\\"k8s/\\\",\\\"k8s/deployments/\\\",\\\"k8s/services/\\\",\\\"k8s/ingress/\\\",\\\"k8s/helm/\\\",\\\"scripts/\\\",\\\"tests/\\\"],\\\"deployment\\\":\\\"Docker Compose for local dev, full multi‑container deployment is on Kubernetes (EKS). ECR stores container images. Each service has its own deployment manifest with resource requests/limits, liveness/readiness probes, and autoscaling. Kafka runs on Confluent Cloud or self‑hosted on EKS with Strimzi. The API Gateway uses AWS ALB/NGINX with TLS termination. PostgreSQL via Amazon Aurora Serverless, Redis via ElastiCache, Elasticsearch via OpenSearch Service. S3 for media storage. CloudFront CDN delivers static assets. GitHub Actions pipeline builds, tests, and pushes images to ECR, then triggers Helm upgrade. Observability uses Prometheus + Grafana for metrics, Loki for logs, Jaeger for tracing. All services communicate via mutual TLS and use Envoy sidecar for service mesh. Continuous security scanning with Snyk and Trivy.\\\"}\",\"generationInfo\":{\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}}]]},\"tokenUsage\":{\"completionTokens\":1486,\"promptTokens\":132,\"totalTokens\":1618}}}"}}
