{"__type":"$$EventMessageAiNode","id":"b5465f84-bac5-428a-bfc2-50bfc9fa1307","ts":"2026-07-18T13:23:05.931-04:00","eventName":"n8n.ai.llm.generated","message":"n8n.ai.llm.generated","payload":{"executionId":"126","nodeName":"OpenRouter Chat Model","workflowName":"ForgeAI - Software Architect Agent","nodeType":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenRouter","workflowId":"GtMVKU0V13n1DZOO","msg":"{\"messages\":[\"System: You are ForgeAI Software Architect.\\n\\nDesign the complete software architecture.\\n\\nReturn ONLY JSON.\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"architecture\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"frontend\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"backend\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"database\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n  \\\"apis\\\":[],\\n  \\\"folder_structure\\\":[],\\n  \\\"deployment\\\":\\\"\\\"\\n}\\nHuman: AI powered travel planner\"],\"options\":{\"openai_api_key\":{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"secret\",\"id\":[\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"]},\"model\":\"openai/gpt-oss-20b:free\",\"max_retries\":2,\"configuration\":{\"baseURL\":\"https://openrouter.ai/api/v1\",\"fetchOptions\":{\"dispatcher\":{\"_events\":{},\"_eventsCount\":0}}},\"model_kwargs\":{}},\"response\":{\"response\":{\"generations\":[[{\"text\":\"```json\\n{\\n  \\\"architecture\\\": \\\"The system follows a loosely coupled microservice architecture with a Service-Oriented Architecture (SOA) layer on top of containerized services. An API Gateway (Kong) handles request routing, security, rate limiting, and OAuth2/JWT authentication. Services include: 1) Auth Service (Node.js+Passport), 2) Search & Recommendation Service (Python FastAPI + LangChain + OpenAI API), 3) Itinerary Planning Service (Python + Neo4j graph DB for travel/matching), 4) Booking & Payment Service (Java Spring Boot + Stripe integration), 5) Notification Service (Node.js + SendGrid/Firebase), 6) Analytics Service (-peer client events). Data orchestration occurs through a Kafka event bus, enabling real‑time updates and asynchronous job processing. Circuit breakers, retries, and health checks are implemented using Resilience4j and custom health endpoints. All services expose RESTful JSON APIs and a limited number of gRPC endpoints forBeneficiary communication.\\\",\\n  \\\"frontend\\\": \\\"SvelteKit front‑end web application with TypeScript, using SWR for data fetching, and TailwindCSS for responsive design. A separate mobile MFA application built in Flutter (Dart) for iOS and Android uses platform specific widgets but shares core state via a shared Dart library. The client uses GraphQL (Apollo) to aggregate data across microservices, with an in‑app AI chatbot powered by the same GPT model via the backend service. Auth is handled via Auth0 or custom OAuth2 flow through the Gateway.\\\",\\n  \\\"backend\\\": \\\"All back‑end services are containerised Docker images deployed in Kubernetes. Services are written in two main stacks: Node.js+NestJS for auth and notifications; Python FastAPI (uvicorn) for AI recommendation, search, and itinerary services. A Java Spring Boot service handles payments, integrates with Stripe and PayPal SDKs. Shared libraries (e.g., validation schemas, authentication helpers) live in a monorepo under /libs and are built with Lerna+Yarn and published to a private npm registry. Deployment pipelines use GitHub Actions to build, test, lint, run unit and integration tests, build Docker images, and push to a registry (ECR or Google Artifactory).\\\",\\n  \\\"database\\\": \\\"PostgreSQL 15 for relational data (users, bookings, itineraries, reviews). Neo4j 5 for graph data (destination connections, recommendation graph). MongoDB Atlas for semi‑structured data (session logs, dynamic content). Redis 7 for caching session state, rate limiting, and message brokering (fallback to Kafka).\\\",\\n  \\\"apis\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"service\\\": \\\"Auth Service\\\",\\n      \\\"endpoints\\\": [\\n        \\\"/api/auth/register\\\",\\n        \\\"/api/auth/login\\\",\\n        \\\"/api/auth/refresh\\\",\\n        \\\"/api köpa/oauth2/callback\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"service\\\": \\\"Search & Recommendation Service\\\",\\n      \\\"endpoints\\\": [\\n        \\\"/api/search/destinations\\\",\\n        \\\"/api/recommend/travel\\\",\\n        \\\"/api/recommend/flights\\\",\\n        \\\"/api/recommend/hotels\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"service\\\": \\\"Itinerary Planning Service\\\",\\n      \\\"endpoints\\\": [\\n        \\\"/api/plans/create\\\",\\n        \\\"/api/plans/{planId}\\\",\\n        \\\"/api/plans/{planId}/ typical\\\",\\nITALY\\\",\\n        \\\"/api/plans/{planId}/stoppings\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"service\\\": \\\"Booking & Payment Service\\\",\\n      \\\"endpoints\\\": [\\n        \\\"/api/bookings/create\\\",\\n        \\\"/api/bookings/{bookingId}\\\",\\n        \\\"/api/payments/initiate\\\",\\n        \\\"/api/payments/callback\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"service\\\": \\\"Notification Service\\\",\\n      \\\"endpoints\\\": [\\n        \\\"/api/notifications/email\\\",\\n        \\\"/api/notifications/push\\\",\\n        \\\"/api/notifications/sms\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"service\\\": \\\"Analytics Service\\\",\\n      \\\"endpoints\\\": [\\n        \\\"/api/analytics/events\\\",\\n        \\\"/api/analytics/metrics\\\"\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"folder_structure\\\": [\\n    \\\"./\\\",\\n    \\\"frontend/\\\",\\n    \\\"frontend/package.json\\\",\\n    \\\"frontend/tsconfig.json\\\",\\n    \\\"frontend/src/\\\",\\n    \\\"backend/\\\",\\n    \\\"backend cage/\\\",\\n    \\\"backend/libs/\\\",\\n    \\\"backend/libs/auth/\\\",\\n    \\\"backend/libs/notification/\\\",\\n    \\\"scripts/\\\",\\n    \\\"scripts/ci/\\\",\\n    \\\"scripts/deploy/\\\",\\n    \\\"k8s/\\\",\\n    \\\"k8s/api-gateway/\\\",\\n    \\\"k8s/auth-service/\\\",\\n    \\\"k8s/search-service/\\\",\\n    \\\"k8s/plan-service/\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"deployment\\\": \\\"Infrastructure as Code via Terraform creates VPC, subnets, Kubernetes EKS (Amazon) or GKE (Google). Helm charts package each microservice, deploying to a dedicated namespace. CI/CD uses GitHub Actions: build -> unit’au integration tests -> Docker image push -> Helm upgrade. Observability stack includes Prometheus, Grafana, Loki for logs, and OpenTelemetry for distributed tracing. HTTPS termination via AWS Certificate Manager/letsencrypt. Auto scaling via Horizontal Pod Autoscaler, and Canary releases via Argo Rollouts. Backups via Velero for persistent volumes. Disaster recovery via multi-az and scheduled database snapshots.\\\"\\n}\\n```\",\"generationInfo\":{\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}}]]},\"tokenUsage\":{\"completionTokens\":1419,\"promptTokens\":132,\"totalTokens\":1551}}}"}}
