fresh tokens, leveraging PKCE for mobile/web clients.\\\",\\\"Enforce the principle of least privilege for all APIs and database interactions.\\\",\\\"Apply strict input validation, output encoding, and parameterized queries to prevent injection attacks.\\\",\\\"Deploy WAF and rate limiting to mitigate DDoS and brute‑force attempts.\\\",\\\"Regularly rotate secrets, use hardware security modules (HSM) or secrets management services, and monitor for secret leaks.\\\",\\\"Adopt a comprehensive SOC 2 / ISO 27001 framework and conduct regular penetration testing.\\\"],\\\"authentication\\\":\\\"Use OAuth 2.0 (Authorization Code Flow with PKCE) for user sign‑in, coupled with multi‑factor authentication (MFA). Store refresh tokens securely using secure storage APIs (e.g., Android Keystore, iOS Keychain).\\\",\\\"authorization\\\":\\\"Implement role‑based access control (RBAC) to delineate permissions for users (e.g., planner, traveler, admin). Use scopes in OAuth tokens to limit API access to only required resources. Enforce approval workflows for data sharing with third‑party services.\\\",\\\"vulnerabilities\\\":[\\\"SQL/NoSQL injection via unsanitized query parameters.\\\",\\\"Cross‑Site Scripting (XSS) from user‑generated content on travel itineraries.\\\",\\\"Broken Object Level Authorization (bOLA) javaScript APIs allowing manipulation of other users’ bookings.\\\",\\\"Enforced session fixation by using predictable session IDs.\\\",\\\"Weak cryptographic storage of API keys leading to credential compromise.\\\",\\\"Unvalidated redirects open to phishing attacks.\\\",\\\"Insufficient logging could hinder incident responseosing未。\\\"}\",\"generationInfo\":{\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}}]]},\"tokenUsage\":{\"completionTokens\":597,\"promptTokens\":126,\"totalTokens\":723}}}"}}
