 rotate third‑party API keys regularly; use dedicated service accounts with minimal scopes\\\",\\n    \\\"Enable logging, monitoring, and alerting for authentication failures, unusual data access patterns, and API usage spikes\\\",\\n    \\\"Conduct regular penetration testing and code reviews focusing on authentication, authorization, and data handling\\\",\\n    \\\"Implement rate limiting and IP whitelisting for sensitive API endpoints\\\",\\n    \\\"Use content security policy (CSP) headers and HTTP security headers (Strict-Transport-Security, X-Frame-Options, X-XSS-Protection)\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"authentication\\\": \\\"OAuth 2.0 + OpenID Connect with MFA; session tokens signed and bound to device/IP\\\",\\n  \\\"authorization\\\": \\\"RBAC with fine‑grained claims; enforce least privilege on API routes; use attribute‑based access control for sensitive data\\\",\\n  \\\"vulnerabilities\\\": [\\n    \\\"SQL Injection (dynamic queries without parameterization)\\\",\\n    \\\"Cross‑Site Scripting (XSS) via unescaped user input in web UI\\\",\\n    \\\"Cross‑Site Request Forgery (CSRF) on state‑changing API endpoints\\\",\\n    \\\"Insecure Direct Object References (IDOR) exposing other users' bookings\\\",\\n    \\\"Weak Session Management (session fixation, long‑lived cookies)\\\",\\n    \\\"Insecure Data Storage (plain‑text credentials, unencrypted DB fields)\\\",\\n    \\\"Insecure Dependency (outdated third‑party libraries with known exploits)\\\",\\n    \\\"Man‑in‑the‑Middle (MITM) due to missing TLS or weak cipher suites\\\",\\n    \\\"API Key leaks via version control or exposed client‑side code\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\",\"generationInfo\":{\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}}]]},\"tokenUsage\":{\"completionTokens\":700,\"promptTokens\":126,\"totalTokens\":826}}}"}}
