{"__type":"$$EventMessageAiNode","id":"cbe9cf96-3b7a-4595-8b6f-e015b960616c","ts":"2026-07-18T13:56:06.665-04:00","eventName":"n8n.ai.llm.generated","message":"n8n.ai.llm.generated","payload":{"executionId":"146","nodeName":"OpenRouter Chat Model","workflowName":"ForgeAI - Documentation Writer","nodeType":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenRouter","workflowId":"vCVI64nqDGv2sLXl","msg":"{\"messages\":[\"System: You are ForgeAI Documentation Writer.\\n\\nReturn ONLY JSON.\\n\\n{\\n \\\"README\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n \\\"installation\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n \\\"folder_structure\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n \\\"deployment\\\":\\\"\\\",\\n \\\"api_documentation\\\":[]\\n}\\nHuman: {\\n  \\\"idea\\\": \\\"AI powered travel planner\\\"\\n}\"],\"options\":{\"openai_api_key\":{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"secret\",\"id\":[\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"]},\"model\":\"openai/gpt-oss-20b:free\",\"max_retries\":2,\"configuration\":{\"baseURL\":\"https://openrouter.ai/api/v1\",\"fetchOptions\":{\"dispatcher\":{\"_events\":{},\"_eventsCount\":0}}},\"model_kwargs\":{}},\"response\":{\"response\":{\"generations\":[[{\"text\":\"```json\\n{\\n  \\\"README\\\": \\\"# AI Powered Travel Planner\\\\n\\\\nAn intelligent travel planning service built with Flask, React, and OpenAI. It helps users generate personalized itineraries, book flights and hotels, and receive real‑time travel updates.\\\\n\\\\n- **Tech Stack**: Python 3.12, Flask, React v18, PostgreSQL, Redis, OpenAI API\\\\n- **Features**:\\\\n  - Natural languageächen itineraries\\\\n  - Dynamic pricing & availability via flight/hotel APIs\\\\n  - Push notifications for travel alerts\\\\n  - Secure user authentication with JWT\\\\n- **Platform**: Web application; future mobile support via React Native\\\\n- **License**: Apache 2.0\\\\n\\\\n## Quick Start cough\\\\n```bash\\\\ngit clone https://github.com/your-org/ai-travel-planner.git Try the demo via Docker or a local environment.\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## Contributing\\\\nSee [CONTRIBUTING.md](/CONTRIBUTING.md) for guidelines.\\\\n\\\\n## Roadmap\\\\n- Real-time chéking of flight seat availability\\\\n- Integration with TCA (Travel Cost Analysis) models\\\\n- Voice assistant support\\\\n- AI‑powered visa & documentation helper\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\nFor more detailed docs, visit the [Docs](#docs) section below.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n# Docs\\\\n\\\\n1. [Installation](#installation)\\\\n2. [Folder Structure](#folder-structure)\\\\n3. [Deployment](#deployment)\\\\n4. [API Reference](#api-documentation)\\\\n5. [Testing](#testing)\\\\n6. [Security](#security)\\\\n\\\\n---\\\",\\n  \\\"installation\\\": \\\"# Install Locally\\\\n\\\\n## Prerequisites\\\\n- **Docker** (>= 20.10.0)\\\\n- **Python** 3.12+ (for local development)\\\\n- **Node.js** 20+ and **npm** for the frontend\\\\n- **PostgreSQL** 15+ & **Redis** 7+ running locally or via Docker Compose\\\\n\\\\n## 1. Clone Repository\\\\n```bash\\\\ngit clone https(news)code.com/your-org/ai-travel-planner.git\\\\ncd ai-travel-planner\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n ansin\\\\n\\\\n## 2. Setup Environment Variables\\\\nCreate a `.env` file in the project root:\\\\n```\\\\n# Flask backend\\\\nFLASK_APP=app.py\\\\nFLASK_ENV=development\\\\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/ai_travel\\\\nREDIS_URL=redis://localhost:637 Fabrillee\\\\nOPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...   # from OpenAI\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n**Note**: Keep your `OPENAI_API_KEY` confidential; never commit this file.\\\\n\\\\n## 3. Build & Run with Docker Compose\\\\nEnsure Docker is running, then:\\\\n```bash\\\\n# Build containers\\\\n docker buildx build --platform linux/amd64 . -t ai-travel-planner:dev\\\\n\\\\n下载\\\\n# Run containers\\\\n docker compose up --build\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nAccess the frontend at [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000) and the backend API at [http://localhost:5000](http://localhost:5000).\\\\n\\\\n## 4. Run Locally (without Docker)\\\\n### Backend\\\\n```bash\\\\npython3 -m venv .venv\\\\nsource .venv/bin/activate\\\\npip install -r requirements.txt\\\\nflask run\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Frontend\\\\n```bash\\\\ncd frontend\\\\nnpm install\\\\nnpm start\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nscope\\\\n\\\\n## 5. Seed Database\\\\n```bash\\\\nflask db upgrade\\\\nflask seeddb);\\r\\n\\r\\n// Use the seeddb script to pre-load spotlightable datasets\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\nFor more advanced deployment, see the [Deployment] section.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\",\\n  \\\"folder_structure\\\": \\\"# Project Folder Structure\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\nai-travel-planner/\\\\n├── backend/                  # Flask API code\\\\n│   ├── app.py                # Entry point\\\\n│   ├── config.py             # Configuration & env handling\\\\n│   ├── requirements.txt      # Python dependencies\\\\n│   ├── migrations/           # Alembic migrations\\\\n│   ├── models/               # SQLAlchemy models\\\\n│   ├── routes/               # Flask Blueprint modules\\\\n│   ├── services/             # Business logic & OpenAI wrappers\\\\n│   ├── utils/                # Helpers (e.g., caching, error handling)\\\\n│   └── tests/                # Unit & integration tests\\\\n├── frontend/                 # React SPA\\\\n│   ├── public/\\\\n│   ├── src/\\\\n│   │   ├── components/\\\\n│   │   ├── pages/\\\\n│   │   ├── services/       # API client wrappers\\\\n│   │   ├── hooks/          # Custom React hooks\\\\n│   │   └── App.js\\\\n│   ├── package.json\\\\n│   └── vite.config.js\\\\n├── docker/                   # Dockerfiles and compose\\\\n│   ├── Dockerfile.backend\\\\n│   ├── Dockerfile.frontend\\\\n│   └── docker-compose.yml\\\\n├── scripts/                  # Helper scripts (seeding, migrations, etc.)\\\\n├── .env.example\\\\n├── .gitignore\\\\n├── README.md\\\\n└── CONTRIBUTING.md\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n* **backend**: Core API logic, authentication, DB models.\\\\n* **frontend**: User interface, navigation, state management.\\\\n* **docker**: Immutable container definitions for reproducible builds.\\\\n* **scripts**: Utility scripts for database seeding and maintenance tasks.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\",\\n  \\\"deployment\\\": \\\"# Deployment Guide\\\\n\\\\nThe application is container‑oriented, making it suitable for cloud platforms such as AWS ECS/EKS, GCP Cloud Run, Azure Container Instances, or DigitalOcean App Platform.\\\\n\\\\n## 1. Containerization\\\\n\\\\nAll containers are built with multi‑stage builds for minimal image size.\\\\n\\\\n**Dockerfile.backend**:\\\\n```Dockerfile\\\\nFROM python:3.12-slim AS builder\\\\nWORKDIR /appруст\\\\nRUN pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt\\\\nCOPY . /app\\\\nFROM python:3.12-slim\\\\nWORKDIR /app\\\\nCOPY --from=builder /app /app\\\\nENV FLASK_ENV=production\\\\nCMD [\\\\\\\"gunicorn\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"app:app\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"-w\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"4\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"-b\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"0.0.0.0:5000\\\\\\\"]\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n**Dockerfile.frontend**:\\\\n```Dockerfile\\\\nFROM node:20-alpine AS builder\\\\nWORKDIR /app\\\\nCOPY frontend/package*.json ./\\\\nRUN npm ci\\\\nCOPY frontend/ .\\\\nRUN npm run build\\\\nFROM nginx:stable-alpine\\\\nCOPY --from=builder /app/dist /usr/share/nginx/html\\\\nEXPOSE 80\\\\nENTRYPOINT [\\\\\\\"nginx\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"-g\\\\\\\",,de\\\\\\\"daemon off;\\\\\\\"]\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## 2. Cloud Provider Setup\\\\n\\\\n### Amazon ECS/EKS\\\\n1. Push images to ECR.\\\\n2. Create an ECS Service with Fargate launch type, defining CPU/dao.\\\\n3. Add RDS PostgreSQL instance and ElastiCache Redis cluster.\\\\n4. Use Parameter Store or Secrets Manager for env vars.\\\\n5. Configure Application Load Balancer to route `/api/*` to backend and `/` to frontend.\\\\n6. Enable ECS Service Auto‑Scaling.\\\\n\\\\n### Google Cloud Run\\\\n- Build images with Cloud Build.\\\\n- Deploy each service separately:\\\\n`gcloud run deploy api --image gcr.io/<project>/api:latest`.\\\\n- Use Cloudennig to store secrets.\\\\n- Use Cloud SQL + Cloud Memorystore for DB/Redis.\\\\n\\\\n### Azure Container Apps\\\\n- Push to Azure Container Registry.\\\\n- Create Container App Service with 2 controllers (frontend/back). Use Azure Database for PostgreSQL and Azure Cache for Redis.\\\\n\\\\n## 3. Continuous Delivery\\\\n- GitHub Actions pipeline: `lint`, `test`, `docker-build`, `docker-push`, `deploy` (to the chosen cloud).\\\\n- Example `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`:\\\\n\\\\n```yaml\\\\nname: Deploy\\\\nruns-on: ubuntu-latest\\\\nsteps:\\\\n- uses: actions/checkout@v4\\\\n- name: Login to registry\\\\n  uses: docker/login-action@v3\\\\n  with:\\\\n    registry: ghcr.io\\\\n    username: ${{ github.actor }}\\\\n    password: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\\\\n- name: Build and push backend\\\\n  uses: docker/build-push-action@v5\\\\n  with:\\\\n    context: ./backend\\\\n    tags: ghcr.io/${{ github.repository }}/backend:latest\\\\n    push: true\\\\n- name: Build and push frontend\\\\n  ...\\\\n- name: Deploy toนคร\\\\n  run: ./scripts리에/deploy.sh\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## 4. Security\\\\n- TLS termination via ALB/CloudFront. \\\\n- CORS only allowed for frontend domain.\\\\n- Rate limit with middleware or API Gateway.\\\\n- VPC security groups restrict inbound access.\\\\n\\\\n## 5. Monitoring & Logging\\\\n- Use Prometheus + Grafana (or Cloud Monitoring) for metrics.\\\\n- Centralized logging: Loki + Grafana or Cloud Logging.\\\\n- Alerting on error rates, latency, or CPU thresholds.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\",\\n  \\\"api_documentation\\\":[\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Health Check\\\",\\n      \\\"method\\\": \\\"GET\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"/api/health\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Return server status for monitoring\\\",\\n      \\\"parameters\\\": [],\\n      \\\"responses\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"status\\\": 200,\\n          \\\"body\\\": {\\n            \\\"status\\\": \\\"ok\\\",\\n            \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-18T12:00:00Z\\\"\\n          }\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"User Registration\\\",\\n      \\\"method\\\": \\\"POST\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"/api/auth/register\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Create a new user account\\\",\\n      \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"in\\\": \\\"body\\\",\\n          \\\"name\\\": \\\"email\\\",\\n          \\\"required\\\": true,\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"User email (must be unique)\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"in\\\": \\\"body\\\",\\n          \\\"name\\\": \\\"password\\\",\\n          \\\"required\\\": true,\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Plaintext password (min 8 chars)\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"responses\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"status\\\": 201,\\n          \\\"body\\\": {\\n            \\\"message\\\": \\\"User created\\\",\\n            \\\"userId чыгот\\\"\\n          }\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"status\\\": 400,\\n          \\\"body\\\": {\\n            \\\"error\\\": \\\"Email alreadytechnology\\\"\\n          }\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Login\\\",\\n      \\\"method\\\": \\\"POST\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"/api/auth/login\\\",\\n      \\\"description stranger because\\\",\\n      \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"in\\\": \\\"body\\\",\\n          \\\"name\\\": \\\"email\\\",\\n          \\\"required\\\": true,\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"in\\\": \\\"body\\\",\\n          \\\"name\\\": \\\"password\\\",\\n          \\\"required\\\": true,\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"responses\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"status\\\": 200,\\n          \\\"body\\\": {\\n            \\\"token\\\": \\\"eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1…\\\",\\n            \\\"refreshToken\\\": \\\"eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1…\\\"\\nBis^\\n          }\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"status\\\": 401,\\n          \\\"body\\\": {\\n            बी\\\"\\n          }\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Search Places\\\",\\n      \\\"method\\\": Call,\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"/api/search\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Return a list of travel destinations based on query\\\",\\n      \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"in\\\": \\\"query\\\",\\n          \\\"name\\\": \\\"q\\\",\\n          \\\"required\\\": true,\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Search term (city, landmark, etc.)\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"in\\\": \\\"query\\\",\\n          \\\"name\\\": \\\"region\\\",\\n          \\\"required\\\": false,\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Optional region filter\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"responses\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"status\\\": 200,\\n          \\\"body\\\": [\\n            {\\n              \\\"id\\\": \\\"123\\\",\\n              \\\"name\\\": \\\"Paris\\\",\\n              \\\"country\\\": \\\"France\\\",\\n              \\\"rating\\\": 4.7,\\n              \\\"thumbnailUrl\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"\\n            }\\n          ]\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Create Itinerary\\\",\\n      \\\"method\\\": \\\"POST\\\",\\nCyber,\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"/api/plan\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Generate a personalized 7‑day travel plan\\\",\\n      \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"in\\\": \\\"body\\\",\\n          \\\"name\\\": \\\"destination\\\",\\n          \\\"required\\\": true,\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Destination city or region\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"in\\\": \\\"body\\\",\\n          \\\"name\\\": \\\"startDate\\\",\\n          \\\"required\\\": true,\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"format\\\": \\\"date\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Planned start date (YYYY‑MM‑DD)\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"in\\\": \\\"body\\\",\\n          \\\"name\\\